            <ArticleTitle>Vaginal leiomyoma as a cause of pelvic pain and cystitis cystica.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1330-1</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Leiomyoma of the vagina occurs extremely rarely and may be confused with a variety of benign vaginal tumors. A preoperative diagnosis is seldom made. The author reports a case of leiomyoma found in the anterior vaginal wall beneath the urethra and associated with pelvic pain and urinary symptoms.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
